// "Groundswell": a hymn, and the bass that turns it minor. At 80, in D major and B minor,
// twenty-six bars, about a minute and twenty seconds. Original music, written here, by Claude
// for Ryan. Nothing of any recording or score is quoted.
//
// Written from the wrela-music skill's taste sheet (references/taste.md): the tracks Ryan named,
// the moments in them he loves, and what was found to be happening at each. The brief was only
// "write me a new track", so that sheet is the brief, and this says which of its devices are
// the piece's spine:
//
// - the bass is a character (device 8), and it is the thing withheld (device 1): for thirty
//   seconds there is no bass and no drum, and then both arrive on one downbeat, with no fill;
// - the same material, new weight (device 2): the loud part is the quiet part note for note.
//   The tune, the voices' chords and the bell are unchanged; only the ground under them is new;
// - the cut is the resolution (device 3): the loud part ends off its home chord with the tune
//   leaning, cuts on the bar line, and the quiet chord that follows makes that note sweet.
// Under those: a tune that hovers and is then held (6), a loop of held notes over a walking
// bass with no dominant chord (5), and many quiet parts with a few high piano notes (7, 9).
//
// The concept. A hymn sung over nothing, and then the ground comes in under it. Hushed,
// mournful, heavy. 80 BPM, a slow backbeat, the off sixteenths swung a little (58%).
//
// The one bold thing: the key the bass decides. Three voices hold F sharp, A and D, and lean
// up a step and back in every third bar (to G, B and D): D major, G major, D major, an amen.
// A tune is sung over that, twice, in D major. Then the bass's first note is B. Nothing above
// it changes, and all of it is B minor now. The bass walks down a fourth by step, a bar to a
// note, B, A, G, F sharp, and climbs back: B minor with its seventh, D over A, G major, D over F
// sharp, round and round, with no dominant chord anywhere. Everything else in the piece is
// plainer than it needs to be so that this is the one surprise: every note is in the one
// scale, the tune is in eighths and longer, its stressed notes are on beats or an eighth early.
//
// The one thing to remember, the tune. Four bars: two notes a step apart rock, the lower one
// arriving an eighth early and left hanging (the ninth over D; the eleventh over B minor);
// they rock again; and that time the hanging note leaps a fifth onto the last eighth of the
// bar, to B, and holds it a whole bar while the chord under it becomes G and makes it a third;
// then it walks down by step and stops one step short of home, on E. It never sings the D it
// leans toward until the last bar of the piece.
//
//   D (Bm7)           D (D/A)             G                 D (D/F♯)
//   F♯–  F♯ E––  ·    F♯–  F♯ E––  · B~   ~B–––––  A G      F♯–––E––  ·
//
// Chosen from six kinds tried on paper (scripts/melody.py): this one; a note chanted three
// times with a turn under it (nine tenths chord notes, nothing leaning: the safe cell); a leap
// of a sixth up from A and a walk down to D (a face, but it closes on the home note every bar
// and outlines the chord: what would be written for any brief); sighs, G falling to F sharp on
// each first beat (no leap, no air, and a G rubbing against the voices' held F sharp in every
// bar); a quick low figure answered by one long high note (two things to remember, and its
// figure is the chord broken); and one long note a bar (this one's skeleton with no rhythm).
// This one because it is the only one that leaves something owed, its rhythm can be clapped
// back, and the note a listener would miss is plain: the B.
//
// What the tune does in each part (energy out of ten; the level meant, by bar):
//
// - bars 1-2, the room (1; about -30 dB): the voices come in on D major over a cello's D. The
//   bell says the tune's first three notes once, high. The voice sings two notes up the
//   scale, D and E, alone.
// - bars 3-10, the hymn (3; about -22): the tune, twice, plainly and softly, over the voices
//   and the cello: no bass, no drum. The bell puts a note or two in its rests; the second time
//   a viola joins the voices and the bell answers (once with E and D, the step home the voice
//   doesn't take). Halfway through bar 10 everything stops: half a beat of nothing, and the
//   voice sings its two notes alone again.
// - bars 11-18, the ground (8; about -13): the bass and the drums, on the downbeat. The tune
//   again, note for note, sung harder. The bass answers in its rests: in the first bar of each
//   round with the tune's own way down from B (B, A, F sharp). From bar 15 a second voice sings
//   over the tune, on A where it rocks and a third over it where it moves, with a clap and a
//   shaker. In bar 18 the drums and the bass stop after the first beat.
// - bars 19-22, the swell (10; about -11): the leap, widened once: from the hanging E up a
//   seventh to the high D, the tune's one highest note and the hymn's home note, held seven
//   beats, the second voice a third over it, a violin an octave over it. Then the tune's walk
//   down at half its speed: four even half notes, B, A, G, F sharp, with the bass, the bass drum
//   and everyone striking each. The bass has stopped walking: it stays on G, and the last half
//   note, F sharp, is the major seventh over it.
// - bars 23-26, home (2; about -24): the cut, on the bar line, with no fill. The F sharp is
//   held across it, and the voices' D major makes it a third. The bell says the tune's three
//   notes, half a bar late. The voice sings them once more, and this time the hanging E steps
//   down to D, as the bass comes back to play D: the only time it does.
//
// The palette, by role:
//   held        three voices (a pad made to sing); a cello and a viola bowing with them
//   foundation  a bass drum tuned to B, a fat snare and a clap behind the beat, hats, a shaker,
//               a ride in the swell; the bass in two layers, a sub and a round one an octave
//               over it, so the line is there on a small speaker
//   moving      the bass's answers; the shaker's sixteenths
//   lead        a sung lead; a second voice, late; the violin over it in the swell
//   fill        the bell: the electric piano's overtone, high and soft, with an echo
//
// Cut when it was finished: a violin holding D over the whole ground. Soloed it was 12 dB under
// the other held parts, and the swell is stronger for being where the violin first plays.
//
// What it can't do. The tracks it is modelled on are voices, guitars and a band, and the
// engine has no voice: a sung synthesizer stands for one, and a pad for a choir. Their tempos
// lift a little into a loud part, and one session has one tempo. Several are in three; the
// skill's checkers read four only, so this is in four.
//
// No ear has heard it. Measured on the last take: -13.5 LUFS, a peak of -1.0 dB, nothing
// clipped, a crest of 14.6 dB, a tilt of -2.5 dB an octave. By bar the hymn sits near -21 dB,
// the ground near -13, the swell near -11.5 and the second bar after the cut at -27: 8 dB up,
// 2 up, 15 down. scripts/feel.py raises no flags on the whole or on any part (no note struck
// hard, a semitone sounding under 1% of the time, nothing outside the scale); the lead plays
// the tune as written, cell for cell of scripts/melody.py's roll; soloed, the lead has the
// 500 Hz octave to itself by 12 dB, and the bass's upper layer has the 125 Hz one.

use engine::bowed::{CELLO, VIOLA, VIOLIN, bowings}
use engine::drum::{CLAP, Drum, HAT, KICK, RIDE, SNARE}
use engine::pattern::{Feel, Pattern, pattern, struck, swung, tacet}
use engine::perform::{Mark, Performance, Taste, bar, perform}
use engine::score::{Meter, Score, meter, score}
use engine::session::{Master, Session, Strip, session}
use engine::synth::{LEAD, PAD, Patch, SUB}
use engine::tine::{SUITCASE, Tine}
use engine::tone::Shape

pub const TITLE: Text = "Groundswell"
pub const TEMPO: f32 = 80.0
pub const BARS: u32 = 26
/// Where an off sixteenth falls between its eighths: the ghost notes lean.
const SWING: f32 = 0.58

fn four() -> Meter {
    meter(beats: 4, unit: 4)
}

// ---- the sounds -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The bass drum: tuned to B, the note the bass comes in on, and short enough to leave the
/// bass its octave.
const BOOM: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 61.7,
    tone_t60: 0.32,
    sweep: 2.6,
    sweep_time: 0.014,
    drive: 2.4,
    click: 0.2,
    ..KICK,
}

/// The snare: fat and low, tuned to F sharp, its wires ringing a quarter of a second.
const FAT: Drum = Drum {
    tone_hz: 185.0,
    tone: 0.9,
    noise: 1.6,
    band_hz: 1700.0,
    top_hz: 9000.0,
    noise_t60: 0.26,
    click: 0.2,
    ..SNARE,
}

/// A shaker: a short breath of high noise, softer and duller when it is struck softly.
const SHAKER: Drum = Drum {
    noise: 1.0,
    band_hz: 7200.0,
    band_q: 1.1,
    cut_hz: 4500.0,
    noise_t60: 0.06,
    range_db: 18.0,
    soft_hz: 5000.0,
    ring_touch: 0.4,
}

/// A crash cymbal: metal and noise together, wide open, two seconds long. (The engine's own
/// crash, a plate, was new when this was written, and its second hit came out 8 dB over its
/// first at the same velocity; this one's two hits are within 1 dB.)
const CRASH: Drum = Drum {
    metal: 0.8,
    metal_tune: 1.15,
    noise: 0.9,
    band_hz: 6000.0,
    band_q: 0.4,
    cut_hz: 2600.0,
    noise_t60: 2.0,
    ring_touch: 0.0,
    ..HAT,
}

/// The bass's lower layer: the sub, held (it doesn't die away like a drum machine's).
const DEEP: Patch = Patch {
    glide: 0.07,
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.006, decay: 1.2, sustain: 0.7, release: 0.1 },
    drive: 2.4,
    range_db: 24.0,
    ..SUB,
}

/// The bass's upper layer, an octave over it: a triangle and a sine with a little sawtooth
/// under a low filter that a harder note opens, so the line is there on a small speaker and
/// its answers speak.
const ROUND: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.25,
    triangle: 0.6,
    sine: 0.5,
    glide: 0.07,
    cutoff: 430.0,
    open: 1.6,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.3,
    touch: 0.6,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 0.3, sustain: 0.4, release: 0.1 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.005, decay: 0.9, sustain: 0.65, release: 0.1 },
    drive: 1.3,
    lean: 0.2,
    range_db: 24.0,
    voices: 1,
    level: 0.5,
}

/// The voices: the pad made to sound sung, a triangle over a sawtooth with a late vibrato,
/// coming in over a fifth of a second, dark and wide.
const CHOIR: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.3,
    triangle: 0.5,
    spread: 10.0,
    wide: 0.9,
    vibrato: 7.0,
    vibrato_hz: 5.0,
    vibrato_wake: 0.4,
    cutoff: 800.0,
    open: 1.2,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.4,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.25, decay: 1.0, sustain: 0.7, release: 0.6 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.2, decay: 0.8, sustain: 0.85, release: 0.6 },
    ..PAD,
}

/// The lead: sung. A sawtooth and a triangle, two a few cents apart, under a low filter that a
/// harder note opens a long way: sung softly in the hymn it is round and dark (its filter near
/// 1 kHz), and over the ground it has an edge (near 1.6 kHz, 2 kHz and more in the swell). A
/// vibrato comes in once a note is held, and slurred notes slide.
const SUNG: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.5,
    triangle: 0.4,
    spread: 6.0,
    wide: 0.4,
    glide: 0.07,
    vibrato: 11.0,
    vibrato_hz: 5.3,
    vibrato_wake: 0.3,
    cutoff: 680.0,
    open: 2.0,
    touch: 1.6,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.01, decay: 0.45, sustain: 0.5, release: 0.25 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.01, decay: 0.6, sustain: 0.85, release: 0.2 },
    drive: 0.8,
    range_db: 30.0,
    level: 0.8,
    ..LEAD,
}

/// The bell: the electric piano with more of its overtone, played high and softly.
const BELL: Tine = Tine { bell: 0.16, tremolo: 0.5, top_hz: 9000.0, ..SUITCASE }

// ---- the drums --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A drum's part: the bars' text.
fn drum(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Pattern {
    pattern(name, four(), lines)
}

fn silent(bars: u32) -> Pattern {
    tacet(four(), bars: bars)
}

/// The bass drum. Over the ground: on one, and with the bass on the "and" of three; a soft
/// one leans into that in every second bar, and the fourth bar walks into the next with the
/// bass. It stops after the first beat of bar 18. In the swell's last two bars it strikes the
/// tune's half notes.
fn kick() -> Pattern {
    let walks: Text = "X... .... ..x. .... | X... ...o ..x. .... | X... .... ..x. .... |"
    silent(10)
        .then(drum("kick", [walks, "X... ...o ..x. ..x. |", walks, "X... .... .... .... |"]))
        .then(
            drum(
                "kick",
                [
                    "X... .... ..x. .... | X... ...o ..x. .... | X... .... X... .... | X... .... X... .... |",
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(silent(4))
}

/// The snare: two and four, behind the beat, with ghost notes that drag into the bass drum.
/// Nothing in bar 18.
fn snare() -> Pattern {
    let back: Text = ".... X... .o.. X... | .... X... .o.. X..o | .... X... .o.. X... |"
    silent(10)
        .then(drum("snare", [back, ".... X... .o.o X..o |", back, ".... .... .... .... |"]))
        .then(
            drum(
                "snare",
                [
                    ".... X... .o.. X... | .... X... .o.. X..o | .... X... .... X... | .... X... .... X... |",
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(silent(4))
}

/// A clap with the snare, further behind, from the ground's second half; nothing in bar 18.
fn clap() -> Pattern {
    let back = drum("clap", [".... x... .... x..."])
    silent(14)
        .then(back.times(3))
        .then(silent(1))
        .then(back.times(4))
        .then(silent(4))
}

/// The hat: the eighths, the beats a little harder, a swung sixteenth every second bar. It
/// stops after the first beat of bar 18, as every drum does.
fn hat() -> Pattern {
    let two = drum("hat", ["x.o. x.o. x.o. x.o. | x.o. x.oo x.o. x.o."])
    silent(10)
        .then(two.times(3))
        .then(drum("hat", ["x.o. x.o. x.o. x.o. | x... .... .... .... |"]))
        .then(two.times(2))
        .then(silent(4))
}

/// The shaker: every sixteenth, quietly, the off ones softer and late; from the ground's
/// second half, and not in bar 18.
fn shaker() -> Pattern {
    let bar = drum("shaker", ["xoxo xoxo xoxo xoxo"])
    silent(14)
        .then(bar.times(3))
        .then(silent(1))
        .then(bar.times(4))
        .then(silent(4))
}

/// A ride on every beat of the swell.
fn ride() -> Pattern {
    silent(18).then(drum("ride", ["x... x... x... x..."]).times(4)).then(silent(4))
}

/// A crash where the ground comes in, and where the swell does.
fn crash() -> Pattern {
    let one = drum("crash", ["X... .... .... ...."])
    silent(10).then(one.clone()).then(silent(7)).then(one).then(silent(7))
}

// ---- the parts written as notes ---------------------------------------------------------------

fn part(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Score {
    score(TITLE, four()).voice(name, lines)
}

/// `bars` bars of rest for the part `name`.
fn rests(name: Text, bars: u32) -> Score {
    var s = part(name, ["r/1 |"])
    for _ in 1..bars {
        s = take s.then(part(name, ["r/1 |"]))
    }
    s
}

// The ground. The bass walks down a fourth by step, a bar to a note: B, A, G, F sharp, and
// climbs back by A. Each bar is the root, long, and the root again an eighth before the third
// beat (where the tune's hanging note falls); then, in the tune's rest, an answer: a fall from
// the octave (B, A, F sharp: the tune's own way down) in the first bar, the octave alone in the
// second, nothing under the tune's long note in the third, and the climb home in the fourth.
// Two layers an octave apart play it (`GROUND_` the sub, `ROUND_` the layer over it).
const GROUND_B: Text = "b1/4. !mf b1/8 r/8 b2/8 ( a2/8 f#2/8 ) |"
const GROUND_A: Text = "a1/4. a1/8 r/8 a2/8 r/4 |"
const GROUND_G: Text = "g1/4. g1/8~ g1/2 |"
const GROUND_F: Text = "f#1/4. f#1/8 r/8 f#2/8 r/8 a1/8 |"
/// Bar 18: it stops after its first note, and the voices leap alone.
const GROUND_STOPS: Text = "f#1/4. r/8 r/2 |"
/// The swell's last two bars: it stays on G, and strikes the tune's four half notes.
const GROUND_STAYS: Text = "g1/2 g1/2 | g1/2 g1/2 |"
/// The swell's first bar: the ground's first, harder.
const GROUND_SWELLS: Text = "b1/4. !f b1/8 r/8 b2/8 ( a2/8 f#2/8 ) |"

const ROUND_B: Text = "b2/4. !mf b2/8 r/8 b3/8 ( a3/8 f#3/8 ) |"
const ROUND_A: Text = "a2/4. a2/8 r/8 a3/8 r/4 |"
const ROUND_G: Text = "g2/4. g2/8~ g2/2 |"
const ROUND_F: Text = "f#2/4. f#2/8 r/8 f#3/8 r/8 a2/8 |"
const ROUND_STOPS: Text = "f#2/4. r/8 r/2 |"
const ROUND_STAYS: Text = "g2/2 g2/2 | g2/2 g2/2 |"
const ROUND_SWELLS: Text = "b2/4. !f b2/8 r/8 b3/8 ( a3/8 f#3/8 ) |"

/// The sub: nothing for ten bars; the ground twice; twice more as far as G, where it stays;
/// and D, once, under the last bar.
fn bass() -> Score {
    rests("bass", bars: 10)
        .then(part("bass", [GROUND_B, GROUND_A, GROUND_G, GROUND_F]))
        .then(part("bass", [GROUND_B, GROUND_A, GROUND_G, GROUND_STOPS]))
        .then(part("bass", [GROUND_SWELLS, GROUND_A, GROUND_STAYS]))
        .then(rests("bass", bars: 3))
        .then(part("bass", ["d2/1 !pp |"]))
}

fn round() -> Score {
    rests("round", bars: 10)
        .then(part("round", [ROUND_B, ROUND_A, ROUND_G, ROUND_F]))
        .then(part("round", [ROUND_B, ROUND_A, ROUND_G, ROUND_STOPS]))
        .then(part("round", [ROUND_SWELLS, ROUND_A, ROUND_STAYS]))
        .then(rests("round", bars: 3))
        .then(part("round", ["d3/1 !pp |"]))
}

// The cloud: three voices on F sharp, A and D, which never leave but to lean up a step in every
// third bar (F sharp to G, A to B, the D staying) and come back: D major, G major, D major, a
// hymn's amen. With the ground under them the same notes are the chords above. They sit under
// the tune and never on its notes: with the top voice on the tune's own F sharp, a pad and a
// lead on one pitch, the two added or cancelled by the luck of their phases, and one bar came
// out 4 dB softer than the same bar in the take before.
const CLOUD: Text = "<f#3 a3 d4>/1~ | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 | <g3 b3 d4>/1 | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 |"

/// The voices: softly through the room and the hymn (they stop halfway through bar 10); fuller
/// over the ground; in the swell with two more voices on top, and then G major alone, so that
/// the tune's last F sharp is a seventh over its G and not a semitone under one; softly home,
/// where the last bar leaves the D to the lead.
fn choir() -> Score {
    part("choir", ["<f#3 a3 d4>/1~ !pp | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 |"])
        .then(part("choir", ["<f#3 a3 d4>/1~ !p | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 | <g3 b3 d4>/1 | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 |"]))
        .then(
            part("choir", ["<f#3 a3 d4>/1~ | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 | <g3 b3 d4>/1 | <f#3 a3 d4>/2 r/2 |"]),
        )
        .then(
            part("choir", ["<f#3 a3 d4>/1~ !mp | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 | <g3 b3 d4>/1 | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 |"]),
        )
        .then(part("choir", [CLOUD]))
        .then(
            part(
                "choir",
                [
                    "<f#3 a3 d4 f#4 a4>/1~ !f | <f#3 a3 d4 f#4 a4>/1 | <g3 b3 d4>/1~ | <g3 b3 d4>/1 |",
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(
            part("choir", ["<f#3 a3 d4>/1 !pp | <g3 b3 d4>/1 | <f#3 a3 d4>/1 | <f#3 a3>/1 |"]),
        )
}

// The tune. Its first three bars are the same every time it is sung; its fourth is where it
// stops a step short (`TUNE_SHORT`), sings its two notes alone into the ground (`TUNE_ALONE`),
// or leaps to the high D into the swell (`TUNE_LEAPS`). The second F sharp slides to the E,
// which is leaned on where it rocks; the long B slides down through A to G.
const TUNE: Text = "f#4/4 f#4/8 ( e4/4 !accent ) r/4. | f#4/4 f#4/8 ( e4/4 !accent ) r/4 b4/8~ ( | b4/2. a4/8 g4/8 ) |"
const TUNE_SHORT: Text = "f#4/4. ( e4/4 ) r/4. |"
const TUNE_ALONE: Text = "f#4/4. ( e4/4 ) r/8 d4/8 !mf e4/8 |"
const TUNE_LEAPS: Text = "f#4/4. ( e4/4 ) r/4 d5/8~ !f |"
/// The swell: the high D held seven beats; then the walk down at half speed, four even half
/// notes, the last held across the bar line into the hymn's chord.
const TUNE_SWELLS: Text = "d5/1~ | d5/2. r/4 | b4/2 ( a4/2 | g4/2 f#4/2~ | f#4/2 ) r/2 |"
/// Home: the three notes once more, and the E steps down to D at last.
const TUNE_HOME: Text = "f#4/4 !p f#4/8 ( e4/8~ e4/2 | d4/1 ) |"

/// The lead: two notes alone; the tune twice over the hymn, twice over the ground; the swell;
/// and home.
fn lead() -> Score {
    part("lead", ["r/1 | r/2. d4/8 !p e4/8 |"])
        .then(part("lead", [TUNE, TUNE_SHORT, TUNE, TUNE_ALONE]))
        .then(part("lead", [TUNE, TUNE_SHORT, TUNE, TUNE_LEAPS, TUNE_SWELLS]))
        .then(rests("lead", bars: 1))
        .then(part("lead", [TUNE_HOME]))
}

/// A second voice, from the ground's second half: on A where the tune rocks, a third over it
/// where it moves; a third over the high D; a third over the tune's last note across the cut;
/// and a third over its last D.
fn harmony() -> Score {
    rests("harmony", bars: 14)
        .then(
            part(
                "harmony",
                [
                    "a4/4 !mf a4/8 a4/4 r/4. | a4/4 a4/8 a4/4 r/4 d5/8~ ( | d5/2. c#5/8 b4/8 ) |",
                    "a4/4. a4/4 r/4 f#5/8~ !f |",
                    "f#5/1~ | f#5/2. r/4 | d5/2 d5/2 | b4/2 ( a4/2~ | a4/2 ) r/2 |",
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(rests("harmony", bars: 2))
        .then(part("harmony", ["f#4/1 !p |"]))
}

/// The bell: the tune's three notes in the room; a note or two in each of the tune's rests
/// the first time it is sung (bars 3-6 and 11-14), and an answer the second time (bars 7-9 and
/// 15-17), one of them E and D, the step home the voice doesn't take; the three notes again
/// after the cut, half a bar late; and up D major's notes to F sharp at the end.
fn bell() -> Score {
    let first: Text = "r/2 r/8 a5/4. | r/2 d6/4 r/4 | r/2 g5/8 b5/4. | r/2 r/8 a5/8 d6/4 |"
    let answers: Text = "r/2 r/8 a5/8 f#6/4 | r/2 e6/8 d6/8 r/4 | r/4 b5/8 d6/8~ d6/2 | r/1 |"
    part("bell", ["r/1 | f#5/4 !p f#5/8 e5/4 r/4. |"])
        .then(part("bell", [first, answers]))
        .then(part("bell", [first, answers]))
        .then(rests("bell", bars: 4))
        .then(part("bell", ["r/2 f#6/4 !p f#6/8 e6/8~ | e6/4 r/2. |"]))
        .then(rests("bell", bars: 1))
        .then(part("bell", ["r/8 a5/8 !p d6/8 f#6/8~ f#6/2 |"]))
}

/// The cello: D under the hymn, a new bow every two bars; the voices' lowest note over the
/// ground; D again, home.
fn cello() -> Score {
    part(
        "cello",
        [
            "d3/1~ !pp | d3/1 | d3/1~ !p | d3/1 | d3/1~ | d3/1 | d3/1~ | d3/1 | d3/1~ | d3/2 r/2 |",
        ],
    )
        .then(
            part(
                "cello",
                ["f#3/1~ !mp ( | f#3/1 | g3/1 | f#3/1 ) | f#3/1~ ( | f#3/1 | g3/1 | f#3/1 ) |"],
            ),
        )
        .then(part("cello", ["f#3/1~ !mf ( | f#3/1 | g3/1~ | g3/1 ) |"]))
        .then(part("cello", ["d3/1~ !pp | d3/1 | d3/1~ | d3/1 |"]))
}

/// The viola: the voices' middle note, from the tune's second singing.
fn viola() -> Score {
    rests("viola", bars: 6)
        .then(part("viola", ["a3/1~ !p ( | a3/1 | b3/1 | a3/2 ) r/2 |"]))
        .then(
            part(
                "viola",
                ["a3/1~ !mp ( | a3/1 | b3/1 | a3/1 ) | a3/1~ ( | a3/1 | b3/1 | a3/1 ) |"],
            ),
        )
        .then(part("viola", ["a3/1~ !mf ( | a3/1 | b3/1~ | b3/1 ) |"]))
        .then(rests("viola", bars: 4))
}

/// The violin: only in the swell, the tune an octave over the lead.
fn violin() -> Score {
    rests("violin", bars: 18)
        .then(
            part(
                "violin",
                ["d6/1~ !mf | d6/2. r/4 | b5/2 ( a5/2 | g5/2 f#5/2~ | f#5/2 ) r/2 |"],
            ),
        )
        .then(rests("violin", bars: 3))
}

/// A score as a player with `taste` plays it, sitting in time as `feel` says.
fn played(s: Score, taste: Taste, feel: Feel) -> Performance {
    swung(perform(s, taste, [Mark::Hold { at: bar(1), by: 1.0 }; 0]), feel)
}

// ---- the session ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The whole track, ready to play.
pub fn build() -> Session {
    var s = session(
        TEMPO,
        Master {
            gain: 4.0,
            glue_db: -16.0,
            glue: 0.3,
            makeup: 4.0,
            warmth: 1.0,
            ceiling: -1.0,
            room_time: 1.4,
            room_size: 1.6,
            room_db: -4.0,
            echo_beats: 0.75,
            echo_again: 0.4,
            echo_db: -5.0,
            duck_time: 0.16,
        },
    )
    s.drum(
        "kick",
        BOOM,
        struck(kick(), TEMPO, Feel { swing: SWING, loose: 0.001, uneven: 0.03, seed: 1 }, key: 36),
        Strip { gain: -4.0, room: 0.04 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "snare",
        FAT,
        struck(
            snare(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, late: 0.012, loose: 0.002, uneven: 0.06, seed: 2 },
            key: 38,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -7.0, low_cut: 110.0, drive: 1.2, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "clap",
        CLAP,
        struck(
            clap(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, late: 0.02, loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.08, seed: 3 },
            key: 39,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -5.0, pan: -0.2, low_cut: 300.0, room: 0.35 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "hat",
        HAT,
        struck(
            hat(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, late: -0.004, loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.12, seed: 4 },
            key: 42,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -3.0, pan: 0.45, room: 0.1 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "shaker",
        SHAKER,
        struck(
            shaker(),
            TEMPO,
            Feel { swing: SWING, late: -0.003, loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.18, seed: 5 },
            key: 70,
        ),
        Strip { gain: -9.5, pan: -0.5, low_cut: 2000.0, room: 0.2 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "ride",
        RIDE,
        struck(ride(), TEMPO, Feel { loose: 0.003, uneven: 0.1, seed: 6 }, key: 51),
        Strip { gain: -7.0, pan: -0.35, room: 0.2 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "crash",
        CRASH,
        struck(crash(), TEMPO, Feel { seed: 7 }, key: 49),
        Strip { gain: -17.0, pan: 0.25, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.key("kick")
    s.synth(
        "bass",
        DEEP,
        played(
            bass(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, metre: 0.1, legato: 0.04, detache: 0.06 },
            Feel { swing: SWING },
        ),
        Strip { gain: 0.0, high_cut: 1500.0, duck: 5.0 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "round",
        ROUND,
        played(
            round(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, metre: 0.1, legato: 0.04, detache: 0.08 },
            Feel { swing: SWING },
        ),
        Strip { gain: -1.0, low_cut: 100.0, high_cut: 2500.0, duck: 3.0 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "choir",
        CHOIR,
        played(choir(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02 }, Feel {}),
        Strip { gain: -3.0, low_cut: 180.0, high_cut: 6000.0, room: 0.5 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "lead",
        SUNG,
        played(
            lead(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.05, detache: 0.08, jitter_velocity: 0.04, seed: 8 },
            Feel {},
        ),
        Strip { gain: 0.0, low_cut: 180.0, room: 0.3, echo: 0.2 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "harmony",
        Patch { vibrato: 8.0, ..SUNG },
        played(
            harmony(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.05, detache: 0.08, jitter_velocity: 0.04, seed: 9 },
            Feel {},
        ),
        Strip { gain: -10.0, pan: 0.35, low_cut: 250.0, room: 0.35, echo: 0.2 },
    )
    s.tine(
        "bell",
        BELL,
        played(
            bell(),
            Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02, jitter_velocity: 0.08, seed: 10 },
            Feel {},
        ),
        Strip { gain: -8.5, pan: 0.4, low_cut: 400.0, room: 0.45, echo: 0.4 },
    )
    let strings = Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.04, detache: 0.03 }
    let cello_part = cello()
    let cello_played = played(cello_part, strings, Feel {})
    s.bowed(
        "cello",
        CELLO,
        bowings(cello_part, cello_played, 0, -22.0),
        Strip { gain: -9.0, pan: 0.4, low_cut: 120.0, room: 0.4 },
    )
    let viola_part = viola()
    let viola_played = played(viola_part, strings, Feel {})
    s.bowed(
        "viola",
        VIOLA,
        bowings(viola_part, viola_played, 0, -22.0),
        Strip { gain: -13.0, pan: -0.4, low_cut: 150.0, room: 0.45 },
    )
    let violin_part = violin()
    let violin_played = played(violin_part, strings, Feel {})
    s.bowed(
        "violin",
        VIOLIN,
        bowings(violin_part, violin_played, 0, -22.0),
        Strip { gain: -15.0, pan: -0.55, low_cut: 200.0, room: 0.5 },
    )
    s
}
